cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Consilience Is Not Consensus: Framework Commitments and the Coherence of a Biblical Chronology"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James
    name-particle: D.
    family-names: Longmire
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1383-7698"
    email: jdlongmire@outlook.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdlongmire/christian-designism"
abstract: >-
  Charter document of the Christian Designism research programme. Argues that
  the claim that no scientifically coherent path leads to a young universe
  conflates consensus with consilience in Whewell's sense, and that the
  inference from absent consensus to absent coherent alternative is invalid.
  Assesses the programme against Lakatosian criteria, adopts functional
  maturity of origins as its geochronological position, declines accelerated
  nuclear decay as a degenerating auxiliary, identifies the absence of a
  demarcation criterion between created-mature initial state and process
  residue as the programme's severest unresolved difficulty, and specifies
  conditions of abandonment.
keywords:
  - consilience
  - consensus
  - historical science
  - auxiliary assumptions
  - underdetermination
  - research programmes
  - biblical chronology
  - philosophy of science
